  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 1, 'From paper to digital: a transformational journey'. The upper half is a rising staircase of four stages, each an icon and a heading — PAPER, DIGITIZATION, DIGITALIZATION, DIGITAL TRANSFORMATION — joined by arrows labelled 'From paper to digital', 'Improve existing processes' and 'Fundamentally change healthcare delivery'. A vertical axis, 'Data use', runs from 'Limited data use with little to no interoperability standards adopted' at the bottom to 'Greater data use with greater adoption of interoperability standards' at the top; a horizontal arrow beneath is labelled 'Process Optimization'. The lower half is a table with one column per stage (Paper, Digitization, Digitalization, Digital transformation) and five rows: Definition, Examples, Benefits, Challenges and Dependencies. For example, Paper is defined as manually capturing and processing data in paper formats, with examples such as paper register books and tally sheets; Digital transformation is defined as digitally optimizing and driving systems-level change through innovation, analytics and feedback mechanisms, with examples such as algorithms for personalized treatment plans.",
